  "queryImages": [],
  "deprecatedReference": false,
  "deprecatedMatches": {},
  "qid": "43",
  "tip": "<p>When you see a requirement to lower global read latency while keeping the write path unchanged, think <i>read replicas</i>. Load balancers help for stateless services and storage settings affect capacity rather than latency, and full migrations are only right when the question allows re architecture.</p>",
